#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Filtered-Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:202
msgid ""
"``filtered_keyed_controller.cpp``: This is the source code for a controller "
"node that filters keyed sensor data in reception, being the most relevant "
"lines the ones that define the filter expression and Quality of Service "
"settings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Filtered-Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:204
msgid ""
"// Initialize a subscription with a content filter to receive data from "
"sensors 2 to 4\n"
"rclcpp::SubscriptionOptions sub_options;\n"
"sub_options.content_filter_options.filter_expression =\n"
"    \"sensor_id >= 2 AND sensor_id <= 4 AND measurement > %0\";\n"
"sub_options.content_filter_options.expression_parameters = {\n"
"std::to_string(SENSOR_TRIGGER)\n"
"};\n"
"\n"
"// Create the subscription with the content filter options\n"
"sub_ = create_subscription<demo_keys_filtering_cpp::msg::"
"KeyedSensorDataMsg>(\"/robot/sensors\",\n"
"    rclcpp::QoS(rclcpp::KeepLast(1)).reliable().transient_local(),\n"
"    callback,\n"
"    sub_options);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Filtered-Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:220
msgid ""
"``filtered_keyed_sensor.cpp``: This is the source code for a sensor node "
"that publishes keyed sensor data. The most relevant lines are the ones that "
"create the publication with a particular Quality of Service settings that "
"enables the controller to late join the application but still receiving the "
"latest update for every instance with the use of topic keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/Working-with-topics/Topic-Keys/Filtered-Topic-Keys-Tutorial.rst:223
msgid ""
"pub_ = this->create_publisher<demo_keys_filtering_cpp::msg::"
"KeyedSensorDataMsg>(\n"
"    \"/robot/sensors\",\n"
"    rclcpp::QoS(rclcpp::KeepLast(1)).reliable().transient_local());"
msgstr ""

